1
00:01:46,859 --> 00:01:49,458
(Episode 11)

2
00:01:49,459 --> 00:01:51,059
(This is a work of fiction.)

3
00:02:01,819 --> 00:02:03,619
What brings you here?
Do you miss me?

4
00:02:13,059 --> 00:02:14,179
What is it?

5
00:02:20,379 --> 00:02:21,459
How are you feeling?

6
00:02:21,939 --> 00:02:22,979
I'm fine.

7
00:02:23,699 --> 00:02:25,339
Fat is with me every day.

8
00:02:26,299 --> 00:02:28,259
He takes care of the housework.

9
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:31,819
He even cooks soup, rice,
and Chinese medicine for me.

10
00:02:31,899 --> 00:02:33,259
I only eat and sleep.

11
00:02:35,459 --> 00:02:36,859
When is your follow-up checkup?

12
00:02:37,859 --> 00:02:40,379
I'm taking the medicine
prescribed by Physician Wong.

13
00:02:40,899 --> 00:02:43,619
He said not to mix it
with Western medicine.

14
00:02:45,619 --> 00:02:46,619
Did you find Lok?

15
00:02:47,339 --> 00:02:48,339
Of course I did.

16
00:02:48,899 --> 00:02:50,019
So it's all settled?

17
00:02:53,139 --> 00:02:54,259
Who else can it be?

18
00:02:55,099 --> 00:02:56,099
I don't know.

19
00:03:01,539 --> 00:03:03,779
Chan Fat, long time no see.

20
00:03:04,779 --> 00:03:05,899
What are you all doing here?

21
00:03:05,979 --> 00:03:07,219
I asked them to come.

22
00:03:08,779 --> 00:03:10,579
You're the one who knows them,

23
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:12,699
but you asked them to come?

24
00:03:14,259 --> 00:03:16,019
You must be tired. Take a nap first.

25
00:03:16,339 --> 00:03:18,259
Leave it to me.
Be good, listen to me.

26
00:03:18,339 --> 00:03:19,379
I asked them to come...

27
00:03:20,219 --> 00:03:22,499
because I want you to know
who your husband really is.

28
00:03:26,859 --> 00:03:29,659
I met Chan Fat
at a nightclub five years ago.

29
00:03:29,739 --> 00:03:32,659
He knocked me up and said
he would take responsibility.

30
00:03:32,739 --> 00:03:34,379
Then he disappeared the next day.

31
00:03:34,459 --> 00:03:36,059
He even stole my luxury watch.

32
00:03:36,539 --> 00:03:38,499
This jerk was a total freeloader.

33
00:03:38,579 --> 00:03:40,459
He brought a woman over
while I was at work.

34
00:03:40,539 --> 00:03:42,019
He treated my home like a hotel.

35
00:03:42,259 --> 00:03:44,099
He was unhappy
when I kicked him out.

36
00:03:44,179 --> 00:03:45,979
So he used my name
to borrow from loan sharks.

37
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:47,739
I ended up getting splashed
with red paint.

38
00:03:47,899 --> 00:03:49,538
He said he wanted
to open a restaurant...

39
00:03:49,539 --> 00:03:50,899
and coaxed me into funding him.

40
00:03:50,979 --> 00:03:53,979
I borrowed and borrowed,
over and over again.

41
00:03:54,059 --> 00:03:55,899
I even had to work as a prostitute.

42
00:03:55,979 --> 00:03:58,099
Once he bled me dry, he vanished.

43
00:03:58,579 --> 00:04:00,179
That's crazy! I never did that.

44
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:02,339
They're just bitter
because I left them.

45
00:04:02,419 --> 00:04:03,939
They're making up lies
to slander me.

46
00:04:04,699 --> 00:04:06,819
Honey, I never did those things.

47
00:04:07,139 --> 00:04:10,379
Your niece brought these women here
to frame me.

48
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:12,459
Don't listen to them.

49
00:04:12,699 --> 00:04:13,699
Wake up.

50
00:04:14,459 --> 00:04:15,659
You're just like these women.

51
00:04:16,139 --> 00:04:17,539
Chan Fat is only after your money.

52
00:04:18,659 --> 00:04:19,699
Don't believe her.

53
00:04:20,299 --> 00:04:22,059
You know I love you, right?

54
00:04:22,379 --> 00:04:23,379
I love you.

55
00:04:28,099 --> 00:04:30,699
Whatever she's paying you,
I'll double it.

56
00:04:34,019 --> 00:04:35,019
Fine.

57
00:04:35,579 --> 00:04:36,579
Fine.

58
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:38,259
See? They're colluding to frame me.

59
00:04:39,259 --> 00:04:40,739
I did pay them to come here,

60
00:04:41,259 --> 00:04:43,339
but everything they said is true.

61
00:04:44,699 --> 00:04:46,419
These are just three of them.

62
00:04:46,659 --> 00:04:47,739
His reputation is terrible.

63
00:04:47,779 --> 00:04:48,979
He's a dangerous man.

64
00:04:49,979 --> 00:04:53,059
He only married you for your money.

65
00:04:54,139 --> 00:04:55,299
He told me at the hospital...

66
00:04:55,579 --> 00:04:57,379
that he would divorce you
for 15 million.

67
00:04:58,339 --> 00:04:59,739
He has stuck to you 24 hours a day.

68
00:04:59,819 --> 00:05:01,579
Do you think
he really wants to care for you?

69
00:05:01,779 --> 00:05:04,179
He's manipulating you
to keep me away.

70
00:05:04,939 --> 00:05:07,219
He doesn't want you to have surgery
so you'll die sooner.

71
00:05:07,579 --> 00:05:09,459
Once you're dead,
he gets your assets.

72
00:05:09,699 --> 00:05:11,139
He has never loved you.

73
00:05:11,219 --> 00:05:13,499
He only loves your money! Wake up!

74
00:05:18,859 --> 00:05:20,059
I know all about...

75
00:05:22,099 --> 00:05:23,379
the things he did in the past.

76
00:05:27,219 --> 00:05:28,739
You didn't like my boyfriends.

77
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:31,739
You were afraid I would leave you,

78
00:05:32,299 --> 00:05:35,139
so you used tricks
to drive them away.

79
00:05:36,139 --> 00:05:39,019
But what about you?
Didn't you abandon me too?

80
00:05:39,259 --> 00:05:40,298
You're so selfish.

81
00:05:40,299 --> 00:05:42,619
You're still as selfish as ever.

82
00:05:42,779 --> 00:05:44,339
I drove your boyfriends away...

83
00:05:44,419 --> 00:05:46,019
because you're a magnet
for scumbags.

84
00:05:46,099 --> 00:05:48,739
You get cheated repeatedly
and never learn your lesson.

85
00:05:49,979 --> 00:05:51,419
If I hadn't chased them away,

86
00:05:51,739 --> 00:05:53,259
you would have been left
with nothing.

87
00:05:53,339 --> 00:05:54,699
I won't believe you anymore.

88
00:05:55,219 --> 00:05:56,579
Aren't you just the same?

89
00:05:56,659 --> 00:05:58,499
You flew away
as soon as you grew wings.

90
00:05:58,619 --> 00:06:01,139
I finally have someone
to be with now.

91
00:06:01,219 --> 00:06:03,179
Why won't you let me be happy?

92
00:06:03,659 --> 00:06:05,299
It matters
who you spend your life with.

93
00:06:05,819 --> 00:06:08,579
You can't just settle for anyone.

94
00:06:09,579 --> 00:06:11,819
I only want what's best for you.
Do you understand?

95
00:06:11,899 --> 00:06:13,499
That act doesn't work on me anymore.

96
00:06:13,699 --> 00:06:15,339
I don't want to see you. Get out!

97
00:06:17,939 --> 00:06:20,139
I said get out!

98
00:06:21,819 --> 00:06:22,819
Ignore her.

99
00:06:24,419 --> 00:06:27,019
Go. Leave.

100
00:06:28,779 --> 00:06:30,019
Get out!

101
00:06:30,179 --> 00:06:31,979
Don't be angry. Calm down.

102
00:06:44,819 --> 00:06:45,979
I'm glad you're back.

103
00:06:48,739 --> 00:06:49,979
Regarding Wong Suet Mui's case,

104
00:06:50,019 --> 00:06:53,019
after her boyfriend,
Chow Kwai Hing, passed away,

105
00:06:53,099 --> 00:06:55,259
he left her a safe-deposit box key.

106
00:06:55,579 --> 00:06:57,298
He said he would
leave everything inside...

107
00:06:57,299 --> 00:06:58,859
and his inheritance to her.

108
00:06:59,219 --> 00:07:01,299
Now, Chow Kwai Hing's
ex-wife's daughter...

109
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:02,939
is back to fight
for the inheritance.

110
00:07:04,059 --> 00:07:07,219
But Chow Kwai Hing was
an old man on social security.

111
00:07:07,299 --> 00:07:08,779
How much money could he have?

112
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:10,339
Why would she fight for that?

113
00:07:13,339 --> 00:07:15,899
He has tens of millions
in physical stocks in the safe.

114
00:07:17,299 --> 00:07:18,619
Of course she would fight for it.

115
00:07:19,259 --> 00:07:20,619
How did you know without looking?

116
00:07:21,019 --> 00:07:22,219
Did Tony tell you?

117
00:07:26,779 --> 00:07:29,259
Or should we call Wong Suet Mui in
for a talk now?

118
00:07:29,939 --> 00:07:31,219
As you wish.

119
00:08:01,699 --> 00:08:02,699
Where are we going?

120
00:08:03,979 --> 00:08:04,979
It doesn't matter.

121
00:08:06,619 --> 00:08:07,939
I just want some peace and quiet.

122
00:08:09,579 --> 00:08:12,619
Then let's go to a place
that will make you happy.

123
00:08:27,579 --> 00:08:28,579
Come in.

124
00:08:28,939 --> 00:08:29,939
What's this?

125
00:08:56,659 --> 00:09:02,939
(Toy Shelter by Yau Yam Yam)

126
00:09:22,379 --> 00:09:24,659
These plushies were collected
in your name.

127
00:09:25,379 --> 00:09:27,099
After we clean them up,

128
00:09:27,179 --> 00:09:28,899
we'll give them to children in need.

129
00:09:29,899 --> 00:09:31,379
Of course, you're the founder.

130
00:09:31,659 --> 00:09:33,299
You can take whichever one you like.

131
00:09:34,619 --> 00:09:36,779
I hope seeing these plushies
will cheer you up.

132
00:09:40,099 --> 00:09:41,459
I think you'll like this one.

133
00:09:47,499 --> 00:09:48,859
Why are you doing this?

134
00:09:49,419 --> 00:09:50,539
To accumulate merit for you.

135
00:09:51,899 --> 00:09:53,299
I don't want you to die so soon.

136
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:01,939
- How much?
- It's free. Just take it.

137
00:10:02,659 --> 00:10:04,659
No, I mean how much
did it cost to set all this up?

138
00:10:05,499 --> 00:10:06,499
I haven't counted.

139
00:10:09,539 --> 00:10:10,819
Just consider it my request.

140
00:10:16,739 --> 00:10:18,699
Why won't you ever
accept my kindness?

141
00:10:22,179 --> 00:10:23,739
I don't want
to make things complicated.

142
00:10:25,099 --> 00:10:26,299
Money is the simplest thing.

143
00:10:27,739 --> 00:10:29,035
I don't understand.
I like you, and you like me.

144
00:10:29,059 --> 00:10:30,139
How complicated can it be?

145
00:10:31,739 --> 00:10:33,659
I didn't use to think
it was this complicated.

146
00:10:34,979 --> 00:10:36,419
When I thought I was dying,

147
00:10:37,619 --> 00:10:39,619
I broke down my walls
and gave my heart away.

148
00:10:41,379 --> 00:10:44,419
But whether it's family or a lover,

149
00:10:45,259 --> 00:10:46,419
I always end up getting hurt.

150
00:10:48,619 --> 00:10:50,339
I don't want to talk
about feelings anymore.

151
00:10:51,779 --> 00:10:53,459
I just don't want to get hurt again.

152
00:10:55,299 --> 00:10:58,419
I would rather keep it simple
and just talk about money.

153
00:11:04,379 --> 00:11:05,779
Don't you think I'm foolish?

154
00:11:08,379 --> 00:11:10,979
I've done so much
to prolong my life,

155
00:11:13,819 --> 00:11:15,779
but in the end,
I don't know what for.

156
00:11:25,619 --> 00:11:28,659
I'll use this money
as an operating fund.

157
00:11:30,139 --> 00:11:31,819
This shelter will
grow bigger and bigger.

158
00:11:33,099 --> 00:11:34,859
Your merits will continue
to accumulate.

159
00:11:36,979 --> 00:11:38,299
I won't let you die so soon.

160
00:11:40,619 --> 00:11:42,539
There are many people
in this world who need you.

161
00:11:43,739 --> 00:11:45,659
The toys and me.

162
00:11:48,539 --> 00:11:49,579
If you're not here,

163
00:11:50,459 --> 00:11:51,699
how can I make extra money?

164
00:12:00,059 --> 00:12:03,779
I truly hope you'll continue
to be mean to me, bully me,

165
00:12:07,819 --> 00:12:08,819
scold me,

166
00:12:10,619 --> 00:12:11,819
and say things you don't mean.

167
00:12:16,859 --> 00:12:18,019
Because I believe...

168
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:23,139
Yau Yam Yam is a good person.

169
00:12:26,939 --> 00:12:28,579
As long as you keep living,

170
00:12:31,659 --> 00:12:33,819
you will find someone
who truly loves you.

171
00:12:45,979 --> 00:12:46,979
Or maybe...

172
00:12:48,699 --> 00:12:50,579
that person has already appeared.

173
00:14:11,059 --> 00:14:13,219
Don't misunderstand.
It's just a transaction.

174
00:14:58,139 --> 00:15:00,939
Grandpa? Grandma?

175
00:15:03,859 --> 00:15:04,939
Are you here?

176
00:15:11,899 --> 00:15:12,899
I'm sorry.

177
00:15:14,579 --> 00:15:16,299
I can't find your grandparents.

178
00:15:17,899 --> 00:15:18,899
Actually,

179
00:15:20,699 --> 00:15:22,139
how long have they been gone?

180
00:15:23,179 --> 00:15:24,379
It has been 25 years.

181
00:15:25,739 --> 00:15:26,899
25 years.

182
00:15:29,819 --> 00:15:31,459
They might have
been reincarnated already.

183
00:15:32,179 --> 00:15:34,299
But I only saw them recently.

184
00:15:34,859 --> 00:15:35,859
They even told me...

185
00:15:36,059 --> 00:15:38,539
This is the last time
we'll visit you.

186
00:15:39,299 --> 00:15:42,059
Stop wishing to see us.

187
00:15:42,339 --> 00:15:43,979
You're wasting your birthday wishes.

188
00:15:44,979 --> 00:15:47,299
We hope you'll be happy
in the future.

189
00:15:48,139 --> 00:15:49,859
Truly happy.

190
00:15:50,459 --> 00:15:53,379
Only when you're happy
can we leave in peace.

191
00:16:01,379 --> 00:16:03,579
So they came to see me last month...

192
00:16:06,059 --> 00:16:07,739
because they were going
to be reincarnated.

193
00:16:08,859 --> 00:16:10,259
They came to see me one last time.

194
00:16:12,099 --> 00:16:14,619
Your grandparents didn't do
anything bad when they were alive.

195
00:16:15,859 --> 00:16:17,539
And you burned
so much joss paper for them.

196
00:16:19,259 --> 00:16:21,099
Normally, they would
have left long ago.

197
00:16:24,339 --> 00:16:27,859
But they waited for 25 years.

198
00:16:30,179 --> 00:16:32,059
They must have been
very reluctant to leave you.

199
00:16:55,379 --> 00:16:56,379
What's wrong?

200
00:17:02,139 --> 00:17:03,579
I miss my grandparents.

201
00:17:04,419 --> 00:17:05,539
Did you dream of them?

202
00:17:07,859 --> 00:17:09,859
I don't think
I'll dream of them again.

203
00:17:11,219 --> 00:17:13,019
I'll go pay respects to them
with you one day.

204
00:17:13,619 --> 00:17:15,499
I haven't visited my mom
for a long time either.

205
00:17:20,859 --> 00:17:21,859
I ordered delivery.

206
00:17:34,099 --> 00:17:35,099
Thank you.

207
00:17:48,819 --> 00:17:50,219
Here's 20 dollars. Keep the change.

208
00:17:50,539 --> 00:17:52,299
Seeing you
dressed so formally for work,

209
00:17:53,019 --> 00:17:54,019
it must be hard on you.

210
00:17:54,939 --> 00:17:56,339
- Thank you.
- Do you live here?

211
00:17:57,139 --> 00:17:59,419
Yes, 22C.
You've got the right place.

212
00:17:59,499 --> 00:18:00,499
What's going on?

213
00:18:06,099 --> 00:18:07,099
Master?

214
00:18:14,099 --> 00:18:15,099
22C?

215
00:18:26,979 --> 00:18:27,979
Thank you.

216
00:18:30,619 --> 00:18:32,899
Try this black truffle and egg
pineapple bun.

217
00:18:32,979 --> 00:18:33,979
It's delicious.

218
00:18:34,219 --> 00:18:36,019
He doesn't like fusion food.

219
00:18:36,819 --> 00:18:37,819
Just try something new.

220
00:18:39,019 --> 00:18:40,979
It depends on whether it suits you.

221
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:44,339
Pineapple buns are high
in sugar and fat.

222
00:18:44,739 --> 00:18:47,579
The eggs are made
with whole milk and lots of oil.

223
00:18:47,979 --> 00:18:49,299
It will take a while to burn off.

224
00:18:50,099 --> 00:18:51,739
Trying new things is fine
once in a while,

225
00:18:52,779 --> 00:18:54,579
but it's better
to stick to healthy food.

226
00:18:56,659 --> 00:18:58,299
I'm young. I can afford it.

227
00:19:06,139 --> 00:19:09,019
So Amber likes mature men like you.

228
00:19:10,939 --> 00:19:12,699
No wonder she kept rejecting me.

229
00:19:13,899 --> 00:19:15,939
She rejected you,
yet you stayed the night here?

230
00:19:17,059 --> 00:19:18,299
Those are two different things.

231
00:19:19,699 --> 00:19:20,819
Why did you come to see me?

232
00:19:22,819 --> 00:19:23,819
No reason.

233
00:19:29,259 --> 00:19:30,259
Hello?

234
00:19:31,739 --> 00:19:32,779
I'll be right back.

235
00:19:36,699 --> 00:19:37,979
I have to go back to the office.

236
00:19:38,379 --> 00:19:40,139
- Can you give me a ride?
- Of course.

237
00:19:41,339 --> 00:19:42,339
Make yourself at home.

238
00:19:43,179 --> 00:19:44,179
I'll wait for your call.

239
00:19:45,259 --> 00:19:46,259
Bye.

240
00:20:06,699 --> 00:20:07,699
Hello.

241
00:20:14,579 --> 00:20:16,675
(Negotiate with Shek Chung
for more time in the mortal world.)

242
00:20:16,699 --> 00:20:18,218
(Find out who killed me.)

243
00:20:18,219 --> 00:20:20,539
(Chiu Man Wah, Chan Shuk Ching,
Liu Chi Wai, Tsang Hei Lok)

244
00:20:29,659 --> 00:20:30,979
How long have you been with him?

245
00:20:34,059 --> 00:20:35,059
Two or three years.

246
00:20:37,739 --> 00:20:41,339
I didn't want to be alone,
so I looked for his company.

247
00:20:45,779 --> 00:20:46,899
But now, sometimes,

248
00:20:49,059 --> 00:20:50,339
I really do want to see him.

249
00:20:56,219 --> 00:20:57,835
I might have been
in a bad mood that day...

250
00:20:57,859 --> 00:20:59,379
and said some unpleasant things.

251
00:20:59,859 --> 00:21:02,459
I'm sorry if there were
any hard feelings.

252
00:21:05,339 --> 00:21:06,339
No need to apologize.

253
00:21:07,379 --> 00:21:08,579
I understand.

254
00:21:10,499 --> 00:21:12,019
To me,

255
00:21:12,379 --> 00:21:14,499
you will always
be a very important person.

256
00:21:16,699 --> 00:21:18,699
I hope you are...

257
00:21:19,739 --> 00:21:20,739
truly happy with him.

258
00:21:31,219 --> 00:21:32,219
Ms. Mui.

259
00:21:34,259 --> 00:21:37,139
Yam Yam, you've grown so much,
I almost didn't recognize you.

260
00:21:37,219 --> 00:21:38,219
Long time no see.

261
00:21:38,739 --> 00:21:40,379
Yes, it has been over 10 years.

262
00:21:41,139 --> 00:21:42,539
Time flies.

263
00:21:43,659 --> 00:21:45,059
Thank you for your help this time.

264
00:21:45,219 --> 00:21:46,219
You're welcome.

265
00:21:46,699 --> 00:21:47,739
This is Solicitor Lam.

266
00:21:47,979 --> 00:21:49,419
And this is my apprentice, Celine.

267
00:21:49,499 --> 00:21:50,739
We'll be handling your case.

268
00:21:51,419 --> 00:21:52,419
Please have a seat.

269
00:21:58,699 --> 00:22:00,099
Just a small token of appreciation.

270
00:22:00,419 --> 00:22:01,779
Fruit is good for your health.

271
00:22:02,139 --> 00:22:03,979
- Thank you.
- Sorry to trouble you all.

272
00:22:04,819 --> 00:22:06,699
I'm going to go over the details...

273
00:22:06,779 --> 00:22:08,299
of your case with you now.

274
00:22:08,659 --> 00:22:10,675
If there's anything
you don't understand or is wrong,

275
00:22:10,699 --> 00:22:11,939
please let me know immediately.

276
00:22:13,379 --> 00:22:14,819
You were with Hing for 10 years.

277
00:22:15,859 --> 00:22:16,995
Although you weren't married,

278
00:22:17,019 --> 00:22:19,099
you lived together
as husband and wife.

279
00:22:19,939 --> 00:22:22,299
Even when he was diagnosed
with pancreatic cancer last year,

280
00:22:22,539 --> 00:22:23,979
you were the one taking care of him.

281
00:22:32,979 --> 00:22:34,139
Keep this safe.

282
00:22:36,699 --> 00:22:38,139
"I, Chow Kwai Hing,"

283
00:22:38,219 --> 00:22:41,259
"leave all my assets
to Wong Suet Mui."

284
00:22:42,739 --> 00:22:45,139
Don't say such things!
You'll be fine.

285
00:22:47,499 --> 00:22:49,219
This is my last wish.

286
00:22:51,139 --> 00:22:52,139
Take it.

287
00:22:52,819 --> 00:22:55,459
What last wish?
Take that back right now!

288
00:22:57,859 --> 00:22:58,859
And...

289
00:23:09,819 --> 00:23:11,219
Everything in the safe...

290
00:23:12,779 --> 00:23:14,019
is for you.

291
00:23:16,099 --> 00:23:18,179
Stop it, I don't want to hear it!

292
00:23:18,459 --> 00:23:19,739
Stop talking.

293
00:23:20,739 --> 00:23:21,739
Listen to me.

294
00:23:24,459 --> 00:23:25,459
This is...

295
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:30,579
the only thing
I can still do for you.

296
00:23:43,139 --> 00:23:45,099
You can't leave me alone.

297
00:23:47,379 --> 00:23:50,419
You absolutely cannot
leave me alone.

298
00:24:10,939 --> 00:24:14,899
Don't go.

299
00:24:18,099 --> 00:24:22,379
You promised to grow old with me.

300
00:24:55,379 --> 00:24:57,459
But it turns out
Hing had a daughter.

301
00:24:58,059 --> 00:25:00,699
She claims she is the rightful heir
to Hing's estate.

302
00:25:01,579 --> 00:25:03,659
So everything Hing left to you,

303
00:25:03,939 --> 00:25:05,539
including this key,

304
00:25:05,859 --> 00:25:06,979
belongs to her, right?

305
00:25:09,659 --> 00:25:11,339
Actually, this case
isn't hard to win.

306
00:25:12,379 --> 00:25:14,699
Even if Hing's will is invalid,

307
00:25:15,299 --> 00:25:17,539
based on the principle
of deathbed gifts,

308
00:25:18,019 --> 00:25:20,019
this key definitely belongs to you.

309
00:25:20,899 --> 00:25:22,275
Actually, the reason
I'm here today...

310
00:25:22,299 --> 00:25:24,219
isn't to ask how to fight this case.

311
00:25:24,939 --> 00:25:26,939
I don't want to fight it.

312
00:25:32,139 --> 00:25:35,219
Please give this key
to his daughter.

313
00:25:37,499 --> 00:25:39,179
But we have
a very high chance of winning.

314
00:25:39,659 --> 00:25:42,939
Yes, my mentor is an expert
in these cases.

315
00:25:44,379 --> 00:25:46,259
Anyway, I've thought it through.

316
00:25:47,699 --> 00:25:48,739
I want to give up.

317
00:25:51,019 --> 00:25:52,459
Can you tell me why?

318
00:25:55,979 --> 00:25:57,339
I was with Hing...

319
00:25:58,539 --> 00:25:59,579
for 10 years.

320
00:26:01,939 --> 00:26:03,179
I endured 10 years of hardship.

321
00:26:07,339 --> 00:26:08,339
Mui.

322
00:26:09,859 --> 00:26:12,059
I'm not off work yet. Wait for me.

323
00:26:12,659 --> 00:26:14,979
My phone is acting up.
It often won't turn on.

324
00:26:15,899 --> 00:26:17,299
I'll buy you a new one later.

325
00:26:18,499 --> 00:26:19,819
I didn't mind that he was poor.

326
00:26:20,379 --> 00:26:22,979
I gave him
whatever he wanted willingly.

327
00:26:23,539 --> 00:26:25,779
I worked night shifts to care
for him during the day.

328
00:26:26,179 --> 00:26:28,259
I spent all my earnings
on supplements for him.

329
00:26:29,139 --> 00:26:31,779
Even when people mocked me
for supporting a man,

330
00:26:32,179 --> 00:26:33,299
I didn't care.

331
00:26:33,979 --> 00:26:35,379
Because I loved him.

332
00:26:38,099 --> 00:26:41,499
I treated him
better than I treated myself.

333
00:26:43,019 --> 00:26:44,699
I did so much for him.

334
00:26:45,619 --> 00:26:47,379
But it turns out
he never trusted me.

335
00:26:48,259 --> 00:26:50,499
He kept so many things from me.

336
00:26:53,659 --> 00:26:54,819
It's terrifying.

337
00:26:56,299 --> 00:26:59,099
It's as if I was living
with a stranger...

338
00:26:59,539 --> 00:27:01,819
for the past 10 years.

339
00:27:05,979 --> 00:27:08,659
Since he was so afraid
I would take his money...

340
00:27:09,259 --> 00:27:11,419
and pretended
to be poor and pitiful,

341
00:27:13,779 --> 00:27:15,859
why did he leave me money
in the end?

342
00:27:16,859 --> 00:27:18,179
I don't want his money.

343
00:27:19,379 --> 00:27:23,059
If his daughter wants it,
let her have it. I don't want it.

344
00:27:31,259 --> 00:27:33,699
I know Hing truly wanted you
to have his estate.

345
00:27:34,379 --> 00:27:35,939
But I really don't want it.

346
00:27:37,819 --> 00:27:39,779
Why don't you take two more days
to think it over?

347
00:27:40,619 --> 00:27:42,219
I've already made up my mind.

348
00:27:42,419 --> 00:27:44,419
I don't want to be troubled
because of him anymore.

349
00:27:44,539 --> 00:27:46,179
I want to put this behind me...

350
00:27:46,259 --> 00:27:47,979
and get on with my life.

351
00:27:50,979 --> 00:27:53,859
By the way, I haven't
seen your aunt in a long time.

352
00:27:54,179 --> 00:27:56,259
Why don't you take me
to visit her one day?

353
00:27:58,059 --> 00:27:59,059
Sure.

354
00:28:00,179 --> 00:28:02,099
But her situation is
a bit complicated right now.

355
00:28:14,379 --> 00:28:15,379
Who are you looking for?

356
00:28:15,939 --> 00:28:18,739
I'm looking for Cheng Fong Ting.
I'm her friend.

357
00:28:19,539 --> 00:28:20,979
She's unwell
and isn't seeing anyone.

358
00:28:22,419 --> 00:28:24,139
Fong Ting, it's me, Mui!

359
00:28:24,219 --> 00:28:25,378
- Fong Ting!
- I told you she's unwell.

360
00:28:25,379 --> 00:28:27,699
- Are you crazy? Get out!
- Fong Ting, are you there?

361
00:28:27,779 --> 00:28:29,019
Mui.

362
00:28:31,779 --> 00:28:33,419
Don't come out. There are germs.

363
00:28:34,979 --> 00:28:36,739
How did you know I was here?

364
00:28:37,339 --> 00:28:39,659
I ran into your ex-boyfriend
the other day.

365
00:28:39,859 --> 00:28:41,219
I forgot his name.

366
00:28:41,419 --> 00:28:43,339
He told me you seemed to live here.

367
00:28:43,419 --> 00:28:44,979
So I came by to try my luck.

368
00:28:46,859 --> 00:28:48,499
- Are you free? Let's get dim sum.
- Okay.

369
00:28:48,579 --> 00:28:51,019
Hey, I said she's unwell.
She can't go out.

370
00:28:51,819 --> 00:28:52,819
Talk at home.

371
00:28:53,259 --> 00:28:55,019
Yes, that's fine too.

372
00:28:55,099 --> 00:28:57,499
We can talk longer at home. Come on.

373
00:29:03,019 --> 00:29:04,019
Chan Fat.

374
00:29:05,059 --> 00:29:07,019
We're from Regional Crime Unit 2A
of Kowloon West.

375
00:29:07,219 --> 00:29:08,219
What is it now?

376
00:29:08,459 --> 00:29:09,875
You're suspected of being involved
in a drug trafficking case.

377
00:29:09,899 --> 00:29:11,139
You're officially under arrest.

378
00:29:11,219 --> 00:29:12,618
It's not his fault.

379
00:29:12,619 --> 00:29:14,355
Didn't you arrest him before
and then let him go?

380
00:29:14,379 --> 00:29:17,819
- Why are you arresting him again?
- Don't interfere. Let go.

381
00:29:17,899 --> 00:29:21,739
- Let's go.
- Let go of him!

382
00:29:23,099 --> 00:29:24,219
Get me out of here quickly,

383
00:29:24,299 --> 00:29:25,339
or we'll go down together!

384
00:29:26,099 --> 00:29:27,099
- Let's go.
- Hubby!

385
00:29:27,139 --> 00:29:29,339
Hubby!

386
00:29:53,259 --> 00:29:55,219
Where's Fat? How is he?

387
00:29:57,699 --> 00:29:59,379
Your health is
what matters most right now.

388
00:30:01,019 --> 00:30:04,419
The doctor said it's serious.
You need surgery immediately.

389
00:30:05,259 --> 00:30:06,939
Yes, nothing else matters.

390
00:30:07,139 --> 00:30:08,779
Take care of yourself first.

391
00:30:10,339 --> 00:30:11,539
You must help him.

392
00:30:12,579 --> 00:30:13,739
Don't play any tricks.

393
00:30:14,539 --> 00:30:16,419
If he's in jail,
I don't want to live either.

394
00:30:16,499 --> 00:30:18,179
I... I'm not having the surgery.

395
00:30:18,859 --> 00:30:21,579
Are you crazy?
How long have you known him?

396
00:30:22,299 --> 00:30:23,699
Anyway, without him, I'm nothing.

397
00:30:24,179 --> 00:30:26,739
He's a scumbag.
You would risk your life for him?

398
00:30:27,099 --> 00:30:29,739
Do you know how miserable it is
to be all alone?

399
00:30:31,179 --> 00:30:32,699
I don't care
what kind of person he is.

400
00:30:32,859 --> 00:30:33,859
I don't care what he did.

401
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:35,179
I can't live without him.

402
00:30:36,339 --> 00:30:38,699
If I have to be alone,
I'd rather die.

403
00:30:38,779 --> 00:30:40,379
Alone? What do you take me for?

404
00:30:40,459 --> 00:30:42,459
Am I not a person? Am I dead?

405
00:30:42,939 --> 00:30:44,939
Only a man counts
as company, but I don't?

406
00:30:45,019 --> 00:30:46,339
You're completely man-crazy.

407
00:30:46,739 --> 00:30:48,819
If you don't help him,
I won't take my meds.

408
00:30:48,899 --> 00:30:50,059
I won't have the surgery.

409
00:30:50,139 --> 00:30:51,755
I'll send you
to Siu Lam Psychiatric Hospital.

410
00:30:51,779 --> 00:30:53,019
Fine, go ahead.

411
00:30:53,099 --> 00:30:55,075
After you send me there,
I'll go on a hunger strike.

412
00:30:55,099 --> 00:30:56,395
If you go on a hunger strike,
I'll force-feed you.

413
00:30:56,419 --> 00:30:57,835
If you play tricks,
I'll tie you to the bed.

414
00:30:57,859 --> 00:30:58,859
Fine, go ahead.

415
00:30:59,179 --> 00:31:01,059
You'll be the one who killed me.

416
00:31:01,339 --> 00:31:03,219
You're insane.

417
00:31:03,859 --> 00:31:05,539
If you want to die, go ahead.

418
00:31:07,659 --> 00:31:08,659
Yam Yam!

419
00:31:11,459 --> 00:31:15,179
Yam Yam!

420
00:31:15,459 --> 00:31:18,379
Are you really going
to leave her and let her die?

421
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:20,179
You saw it yourself. She's hopeless.

422
00:31:21,739 --> 00:31:23,619
She is very stubborn and headstrong.

423
00:31:23,979 --> 00:31:26,019
But for the sake of her raising you,

424
00:31:26,099 --> 00:31:27,139
please help her.

425
00:31:27,219 --> 00:31:29,298
How? She won't help herself.

426
00:31:29,299 --> 00:31:30,299
I can't help her.

427
00:31:31,939 --> 00:31:33,819
Help her get her husband out.

428
00:31:33,899 --> 00:31:35,539
Are you crazy?
I'm not helping that scum.

429
00:31:36,259 --> 00:31:38,899
You're not helping that scum.
You're helping your aunt.

430
00:31:39,219 --> 00:31:42,739
If you don't help her,
she really will kill herself.

431
00:31:42,819 --> 00:31:44,619
If she wants to die,
I can't stop her.

432
00:31:44,699 --> 00:31:47,179
I don't understand
why she's so obsessed!

433
00:31:49,299 --> 00:31:50,779
When she was young,

434
00:31:50,859 --> 00:31:53,739
she felt your grandparents
only loved your mother.

435
00:31:53,979 --> 00:31:56,019
So she kept looking for love.

436
00:31:56,939 --> 00:32:01,219
Unfortunately, she had bad luck
and met the wrong men.

437
00:32:01,859 --> 00:32:03,899
Maybe because she failed
so many times,

438
00:32:04,099 --> 00:32:06,579
now that she has found a man
willing to marry her,

439
00:32:06,979 --> 00:32:08,459
she has become this extreme.

440
00:32:08,899 --> 00:32:10,459
It's not about bad luck.

441
00:32:10,539 --> 00:32:12,179
She just has terrible judgment.

442
00:32:14,739 --> 00:32:17,859
She doesn't necessarily need a man.

443
00:32:18,139 --> 00:32:20,099
She just wants someone by her side.

444
00:32:21,659 --> 00:32:24,219
You were once her only hope.

445
00:32:32,859 --> 00:32:33,859
Did you get a boyfriend?

446
00:32:35,779 --> 00:32:36,779
No.

447
00:32:37,259 --> 00:32:38,259
No?

448
00:32:38,459 --> 00:32:40,899
Then why do you look so radiant?

449
00:32:42,539 --> 00:32:47,219
That girl said she'll make
a lot of money to support me.

450
00:32:47,939 --> 00:32:48,939
Yam Yam?

451
00:32:49,699 --> 00:32:52,019
Didn't you say
she was just a burden?

452
00:32:54,019 --> 00:32:56,779
They say when women
reach a certain age,

453
00:32:56,859 --> 00:32:58,499
their maternal instincts kick in.

454
00:32:58,819 --> 00:33:00,179
I guess it's true.

455
00:33:01,099 --> 00:33:03,779
Men are unreliable anyway.

456
00:33:04,339 --> 00:33:06,619
It's nice to have a daughter
for company.

457
00:33:08,459 --> 00:33:10,659
Let's see how long
you can keep this up.

458
00:33:10,939 --> 00:33:12,099
You're the one who's a flirt.

459
00:33:12,819 --> 00:33:15,219
- I'm a busybody.
- You are.

460
00:33:17,059 --> 00:33:18,059
Hold on.

461
00:33:26,939 --> 00:33:27,939
Fong Ting.

462
00:33:40,219 --> 00:33:42,219
Thank you for taking care
of Yam Yam all this time.

463
00:33:46,739 --> 00:33:48,339
You're quite something.

464
00:33:49,899 --> 00:33:52,339
You actually dared to refuse
to send a single cent back.

465
00:33:52,899 --> 00:33:54,099
I couldn't even reach you.

466
00:33:54,219 --> 00:33:56,579
And now you suddenly show up
at my house.

467
00:33:59,059 --> 00:34:00,059
I'm sorry.

468
00:34:01,299 --> 00:34:04,219
Something came up, so I couldn't
send the money back then.

469
00:34:06,139 --> 00:34:07,139
Okay.

470
00:34:08,299 --> 00:34:09,299
Give it to me now.

471
00:34:14,659 --> 00:34:15,659
Thank you.

472
00:34:21,859 --> 00:34:22,979
Are you kidding me?

473
00:34:23,859 --> 00:34:26,339
You haven't sent a cent for years.

474
00:34:26,819 --> 00:34:29,259
This isn't even enough
to cover interest.

475
00:34:35,979 --> 00:34:37,539
Actually, Eric and I got divorced.

476
00:34:40,139 --> 00:34:41,979
I get very little
in the court-ordered alimony.

477
00:34:42,099 --> 00:34:43,539
I also have to support two children.

478
00:34:44,379 --> 00:34:46,659
I really don't have more money
for Yam Yam's expenses.

479
00:35:00,659 --> 00:35:01,659
Actually,

480
00:35:02,619 --> 00:35:04,979
I came here this time to ask you...

481
00:35:07,379 --> 00:35:08,659
if you could raise Yam Yam.

482
00:35:27,499 --> 00:35:28,499
I understand.

483
00:35:30,979 --> 00:35:32,699
Raising a child is very expensive.

484
00:35:36,219 --> 00:35:37,219
Don't worry.

485
00:35:38,019 --> 00:35:39,219
I'll take Yam Yam with me.

486
00:35:46,819 --> 00:35:47,819
I'll raise her.

487
00:35:59,259 --> 00:36:00,579
Business was good this month.

488
00:36:00,939 --> 00:36:02,099
Let's go out for a nice meal.

489
00:36:09,099 --> 00:36:10,099
Sweetie.

490
00:36:43,579 --> 00:36:45,939
Okay.

491
00:37:04,979 --> 00:37:06,059
What were you doing?

492
00:37:06,539 --> 00:37:08,699
I'm a bit late
because I was shopping.

493
00:37:08,779 --> 00:37:09,939
Let me buy you a drink.

494
00:37:10,979 --> 00:37:11,979
What did you buy?

495
00:37:15,379 --> 00:37:16,819
You bought a plushie?

496
00:37:17,099 --> 00:37:18,739
When did you become so childlike?

497
00:37:18,819 --> 00:37:20,499
My niece likes them.

498
00:37:20,779 --> 00:37:22,659
You really shouldn't
be so nice to her.

499
00:37:22,979 --> 00:37:25,939
It'll be trouble
if you get too attached.

500
00:37:26,059 --> 00:37:27,979
What are you talking about?

501
00:37:28,539 --> 00:37:31,779
She's not yours.
She'll leave eventually.

502
00:37:32,499 --> 00:37:34,579
Nonsense. She's very clingy with me.

503
00:37:35,619 --> 00:37:37,139
You never know.

504
00:37:37,219 --> 00:37:39,219
I'm just afraid
you'll be heartbroken.

505
00:37:39,579 --> 00:37:42,219
A mother is a mother.
No one can replace her.

506
00:37:49,019 --> 00:37:52,179
Look who I brought back.

507
00:38:52,019 --> 00:38:58,099
(My Family)

508
00:39:13,019 --> 00:39:14,819
Where are you going? I bought lunch.

509
00:39:14,899 --> 00:39:16,259
I'm going to the study room.

510
00:39:17,539 --> 00:39:20,499
I'll put it in the fridge.
Heat it up when you're back.

511
00:39:20,579 --> 00:39:22,459
No need. I'll eat
before I come home.

512
00:39:26,299 --> 00:39:29,139
You had grown up
and had your own circle.

513
00:39:29,539 --> 00:39:31,779
Your aunt didn't understand
and obsessed over it.

514
00:39:32,139 --> 00:39:33,579
She thought you were abandoning her.

515
00:39:35,979 --> 00:39:37,299
Where have you been all night?

516
00:39:37,379 --> 00:39:38,739
Do you think this is a hotel?

517
00:39:39,379 --> 00:39:41,299
I told you I was studying
at a friend's house.

518
00:39:41,379 --> 00:39:44,059
Why can't you study at home?

519
00:39:44,419 --> 00:39:45,979
It's too noisy here.

520
00:39:46,499 --> 00:39:48,659
This is my house.
I can do whatever I want.

521
00:39:48,739 --> 00:39:50,899
I provide for you,
and this is how you talk to me?

522
00:39:52,179 --> 00:39:55,659
Yau Yam Yam, stop right there!

523
00:39:55,739 --> 00:39:57,139
Where are you going?

524
00:40:09,139 --> 00:40:10,659
You owe me.

525
00:40:12,539 --> 00:40:13,979
You owe me.

526
00:40:23,019 --> 00:40:25,339
It's so late.

527
00:40:25,419 --> 00:40:26,795
You haven't contacted me
for so long.

528
00:40:26,819 --> 00:40:28,179
I needed some time to get ready.

529
00:40:28,699 --> 00:40:29,979
Are you ready now?

530
00:40:30,859 --> 00:40:31,899
I'm ready.

531
00:40:33,059 --> 00:40:35,219
You're never allowed to leave again.

532
00:40:35,459 --> 00:40:36,459
Fine.

533
00:40:39,459 --> 00:40:42,659
Your aunt knew long ago
that your mom didn't want you.

534
00:40:43,539 --> 00:40:46,379
She feared your mom
would abandon you in the US.

535
00:40:46,459 --> 00:40:47,739
That would have been even worse.

536
00:40:50,059 --> 00:40:52,739
Fong Ting started working
at a very young age.

537
00:40:53,699 --> 00:40:55,459
That's why she's so obsessed
with money.

538
00:40:56,899 --> 00:40:59,419
But she was still willing
to raise you.

539
00:41:00,299 --> 00:41:02,019
It proves how much you mean to her.

540
00:41:04,139 --> 00:41:05,739
Her flaw is that
she's too sharp-tongued.

541
00:41:06,179 --> 00:41:07,619
She's not good
at expressing herself.

542
00:41:07,939 --> 00:41:09,379
She doesn't know how to communicate.

543
00:41:11,979 --> 00:41:13,739
But now she's giving up on herself.

544
00:41:15,579 --> 00:41:16,739
I really can't help her.

545
00:41:18,739 --> 00:41:19,819
You're so smart.

546
00:41:20,139 --> 00:41:22,699
I'm sure you can find a way
that works for everyone.
